# Quality Gates

Lint and test failures are defects. Fix on the branch; do not bypass hooks.

## Dogfooding

ShipGate is a quality-control repo; it must pass its own gates. No carve-outs for "mature" or legacy code.

| Principle | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| Full codebase | Built-in gates and every suite check apply to the **entire** codebase |
| Suite | Dogfood uses `full` from `shipgate.yaml` — not `pre-commit` or `standard` as a workaround |
| No grandfathering | Do not relax thresholds, narrow scopes, or skip checks — fix violations |
| Allowlists | `.shipgate/allowlists/` entries require an exceptional, documented reason |

Canonical verification: `make check-commit` (see `AGENTS.md`).

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `uv run pytest tests/unit -q` | Default deterministic suite |
| `uv run pytest -m integration` | External tools, network, pip install |
| `make check-commit` | Format + full ShipGate suite |

## Rules

- Never use `git commit --no-verify` or `SKIP=...`.
- Default tests must not require external tool binaries.
- Run the smallest relevant command after each risky change.
- Before claiming done, run fresh commands and report actual results.
